From: Dat Tran <t.ng.t.dat@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp25: import only the RAUC variables from the environment

With CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST, U-Boot imports only variables with the
"w" flag from the environment partition. Mark the three variables that
RAUC changes from Linux (fw_setenv) as writeable; everything else, such
as bootcmd and bootargs, then always comes from the default environment
built into U-Boot.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board and product specific configuration]
Signed-off-by: Dat Tran <t.ng.t.dat@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/configs/stm32mp25_st_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/stm32mp25_st_common.h
@@ -14,6 +14,14 @@
 
 #include <configs/stm32mp25_common.h>
 
+/*
+ * RAUC A/B boot: only these variables are imported from the environment
+ * partition (CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST). All others, including bootcmd
+ * and bootargs, come from the default environment built into U-Boot,
+ * which TF-A verifies as part of the FIP.
+ */
+#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC "BOOT_ORDER:sw,BOOT_A_LEFT:dw,BOOT_B_LEFT:dw"
+
 #ifdef CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS
 /*
  * default bootcmd for stm32mp25 STMicroelectronics boards:
